<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Dikwa</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Dikwa is a town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/borno-state">Borno State</a>, north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nigeria">Nigeria</a>, south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lake-chad">Lake Chad</a>. The Sudanese warlord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rabih-az-zubayr">Rabih az-Zubayr</a> made it his capital after conquering <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bornu">Bornu</a> in 1893. After his death in 1900 it became the seat of the Dikwa <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emirate">Emirate</a>, ruled by a branch of the al-Kanemi dynasty under German and then British control, and it became part of Nigeria in 1961.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/dikwa.jpg" alt="Dikwa" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Mr. Snatch · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Round_about_in_Dikwa.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
